{"url": "https://www.ualberta.ca/en/mathematical-and-statistical-sciences/graduate-studies/admissions/english-proficiency-requirements.html", "final_url": "https://www.ualberta.ca/en/mathematical-and-statistical-sciences/graduate-studies/admissions/english-proficiency-requirements.html", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-10-24", "text": "English Proficiency Requirements | Mathematical and Statistical Sciences\nSkip to main content\nFaculty of Science\nDepartment of Mathematical and Statistical Sciences\nSearch Within\nualberta.ca\nPeople\nPrograms\nServices\nQuick Links\nEmail + Apps\nBear Tracks\nCanvas\nFind a Person\nMaps\nLibrary\nNews + Events\nFolio\nThe Quad\nNew Trail\nYouAlberta\nEvents\nProspective Students\nCurrent Students\nAssociations\nAlumni + Friends\nGive to the U of A\nCareers\nIndigenous Initiatives\nAccess, Community + Belonging\nSupport During a Crisis\nAbout\nAbout\nAbout\nWelcome to MATH & STATS SCIENCES\nOur Legacy\nEDI in Mathematical & Statistical Sciences\nDepartmental Awards\nNews\nIn Memory\nEvents\nCareer Opportunities\nDiversity in Science\nGive to Math\nIntranet\nPeople\nPeople\nResearch\nResearch\nResearch\nResearch Areas\nCentres and Institutes\nUndergraduate\nUndergraduate\nUndergraduate\nPrograms\nTransnational Education\nAwards & Scholarships\nCourses\nDecima Robinson Support Centre\nResearch Opportunities\nScience Internship Program\nStudy Abroad\nMathematics Competitions\nStudent Clubs\nContact\nTransnational Education\nTransnational Education\nTransnational Education\nStatistics with CUEB\nApplied Mathematics with Jilin University\nGraduate\nGraduate\nGraduate\nPrograms\nAdmissions\nFunding\nAwards + Scholarships\nStudent Resources\nRegulations + Guidelines\nContact\nOutreach\nOutreach\nOutreach\nAlberta High School Math Competition\nOther Competitions\nClubs\nCamps\nWorkshops\nFor Teachers\nSponsors\nHome\nGraduate Studies\nAdmissions\nEnglish Proficiency Requirements\nIn this section\nAdmissions\nHow to Apply\nDeadlines + FAQs\nCosts\nEnglish Proficiency Requirements\nRegulations + Guidelines\nEnglish Proficiency Requirements\nSince English is the primary language of instruction and communication at the U of A, all applicants must be proficient in English before admission.\nProficiency is demonstrated by:\na satisfactory score on an approved English Language Proficiency examination (see table below), OR\npossession of a degree from a Canadian institution, OR\npossession of a degree from a country or school listed on the Faculty of Graduate Studies Exemption List.\nAccepted Examinations\nThe Department of Mathematical and Statistical Sciences will accept the following examinations (with a satisfactory score) to fulfill English Language Proficiency.\nTOEFL\nMinimum score of 100 (internet based), with a score of at least 22 in each individual skill area.\nTOEFL Codes:\nThe institution code: 0963.\nThe department code: 72 for Mathematics and 59 for Statistics\nTOEFL (Test of English as a Foreign Language) Score\nIELTS\nMinimum score of 7.0 overall with a minimum of 6.0 on each band for admission. The IELTS test must be the academic module.\nIELTS (International English Language Testing System) Score\nPTE Academic\nMinimum overall score of 68 points and a minimum of 59 points in each of the categories:\nlistening\nreading\nspeaking\nwriting\nPTE Academic (Pearson Test of English Academic)\nApplicant Scores\nThe Department of Mathematical and Statistical Sciences:\nDoes not admit applicants who submit scores below the stated minimum.\nDoes not admit applicants who are required to submit a score but fail to do so.\nWill only accept scores that reflect a test date that has taken place within the last 2 years.\nFor students in a region impacted by Pearson, IELTS, or TOEFL test centre closures due to COVID-19, the department will temporarily accept the Duolingo English Test (taken after February 1, 2020) as one of the ways to meet our English Language Proficiency requirements for fall 2022 admission.\nDuolingo English Test score required by the department is minimum overall score of 120, with no subscore below 100.\nContact Us\nAdministrative: mssadmin@ualberta.ca\nProspective Graduate: sci.gradadm@ualberta.ca\nCurrent Graduate: mssgrad@ualberta.ca\nUndergraduate: mssugrd@ualberta.ca\nGraduate Program Intranet\nInstructor Intranet\nResearch Intranet\nDepartment of Mathematical and Statistical Sciences\nCollege of Natural + Applied Sciences\nUniversity of Alberta\nUniversity Commons 5-140\nEdmonton, Alberta, Canada T6G 2N8\n(780) 492 3396\nTerritorial Acknowledgement\nThe University of Alberta, its buildings, labs and research stations are primarily located on the territory of N\u00e9hiyaw (Cree), Niitsitapi (Blackfoot), M\u00e9tis, Nakoda (Stoney), Dene, Haudenosaunee (Iroquois) and Anishinaabe (Ojibway/Saulteaux), lands that are now known as part of Treaties 6, 7 and 8 and homeland of the M\u00e9tis. The University of Alberta respects the sovereignty, lands, histories, languages, knowledge systems and cultures of all First Nations, M\u00e9tis, and Inuit.\nAbout Us\nContact Us\nMedia Relations\nCareers\nNews\nEvents\nGiving\nIn Memoriam\nCampus Info\nMaps\nBuilding Hours\nBookstore\nLibrary\nParking\nMuseums\nRecreation\nAthletics\nStudent Information\nUniversity Calendar\nRegistrar\nStudents' Union\nGrad Students' Assoc.\nResidence\nDining Services\nServices\nEmergencies\nCampus Security\nSupport During a Crisis\nIT Help\nMaintenance Request\nAssociations\nStaff Services\nStudent Services\nAlumni Services\nResearch Services\nTools + Apps\nCanvas\nONEcard\nBear Tracks\nCERegister\nEmail + Apps\nAdministration\nPresident\nLeadership\nGovernance\nPolicies + Procedures\nPrivacy Statement\nReporting\nCompensation Disclosure\n\u00a9 2026 University of Alberta\nProdStage", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://www.ualberta.ca/en/mathematical-and-statistical-sciences/graduate-studies/admissions/english-proficiency-requirements.html#main"], [